        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/dayton_idaho"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Oregon Short Line Railroad arrived in 1890, establishing a station that grew into Dayton’s freight hub until 1961.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/dayton_idaho"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early settlers joined the Weston Ward before creating the Dayton Ward in 1893, reflecting strong LDS Church roots.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/dayton_idaho"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Dayton receives about 19 inches of annual precipitation, most falling as snow that shapes its winter agriculture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/dayton_idaho"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Dayton sits on Cache Valley’s western edge beside Five Mile Creek, nestled at the foot of the Bannock Mountains.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
